          "text": "The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. Updated orphan schema validation in `check_body()` (lines 152-168)\n- Added `\"entries_b64\"` to the allowed fields for orphan body\n- Added validation that `entries_b64` must be a list of valid base64 strings\n\n### 2. Added `_orphan_entries_problem()` function (lines 304-360)\n```python\ndef _orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Validate that an orphan's entries_b64 matches the attested range in pred.\n    \n    Returns None if valid, otherwise a short problem string containing:\n    - 'range' when the count is wrong\n    - 'chain' when an entry's prev doesn't link\n    - 'head' when the last hash doesn't match head_sha256\n    \"\"\"\n```\nThe function:\n- Returns `None` when decoded entries exactly match the attested range (correct count, proper chain linking from `prev_sha256`, final hash matches `head_sha256`)\n- Returns error strings containing:\n  - `\"range\"` when entry count ≠ `to_seq - from_seq + 1`\n  - `\"chain\"` when an entry's `prev` field doesn't match expected hash\n  - `\"head\"` when the last entry's hash doesn't match `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`\n- Also handles missing `entries_b64`, invalid base64, invalid JSON, wrong sequence numbers, and missing predicate fields\n\n### 3. Wired into `cmd_monitor()` (lines 604-607)\nAdded validation call after predicate extraction:\n```python\nprob = _orphan_entries_problem(o, pred)\nif prob:\n    bad.append(f\"orphan entry {o['seq']}: {prob}\")\n    continue\n```\n\nThis ensures that during monitoring, any orphan without valid hidden entries (matching the attested range) is reported as a problem.\n\n### Test Results\nAll 19 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` pass."
